GOVERNANCE PROPOSAL
ID: fix-agent-engine-pass-user-message-2026-03-03
Date: 2026-03-03
Author: Shiva (Claude Code)
Status: PENDING

## Summary

Complete the rings.interpret() fix by passing user_message through
at the call site in agent_engine.py.

## Problem

The previous commit (fix-rings-interpret-context-injection-2026-03-03)
updated context_injector.build_context_header() to accept user_message
and use rings.interpret() for Kart's knowledge query — but agent_engine.py
still calls it without the message:

    # agent_engine.py:184 (current)
    memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(self.username, self.agent_name)

user_message=None triggers the fallback, so Kart still gets
"system state current tasks" every time. The fix is inert until
this call site passes the message.

## Change

### core/agent_engine.py — line 184

```python
# Before
memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(self.username, self.agent_name)

# After
memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(
    self.username, self.agent_name, user_message=user_message
)
```

user_message is already a parameter of this function (visible at line 194
where it's appended to context). No other changes needed.

## Risk Assessment

- **Risk:** MINIMAL
- user_message is already in scope at the call site
- The only behavioral change: Kart gets context matched to the actual
  user query instead of "system state current tasks"
- All other agents (shiva, sean) are unaffected — the interpret() path
  only runs inside the `if agent_name == "kart"` block

## Files Modified

- `core/agent_engine.py` — one line, pass user_message to build_context_header
